 Finish the interaction with the completion callback supplied to the component factory. It resolves the `ctx.ui.custom()` promise and disposes the component. Do not call `OverlayHandle.hide()` on an overlay created by `ctx.ui.custom()`.
 
+For an inline detail view opened by an editor-border badge, pass `{ retainEditorBorders: true }` to `ctx.ui.custom()`. The editor's visible border widgets remain above/below the view, without showing the draft or moving keyboard focus to the hidden editor. A second badge click can call that interaction's completion callback to close it. Keep one pending/open interaction per badge and revoke its callback on session shutdown; repeated clicks must not stack duplicate views. Empty border rows take no space. The option is ignored for overlays and custom editors without `createBorderComponent()` support. Nested confirmation/input dialogs do not retain the rows. Mouse interaction still requires fullscreen mode; preserve command/shortcut and keyboard dismissal paths.
